 "overview": "This file (State Department decimal file 894.428/9-1443, classified under Japanese educational and library affairs) comprises a September 14, 1943 transmittal memorandum from Colonel Truman M. Martin, Chief of the Military Intelligence Division's Japan Branch, and an accompanying 11-page enclosure compiled by R. L. Tuthill consisting of an explanatory preface and a master numerical directory of 169 libraries. The document details a comprehensive wartime military intelligence project that surveyed public, university, and corporate industrial libraries across the United States and Canada to catalogue Japanese-related literature ('Japonica') of military, economic, and scientific value. The resulting card catalogue, prepared by the New York Office of MID and the ISO-TS Library, was distributed to and coordinated among the War Department (A-2), the Department of State, and the Department of Commerce to support the Allied war effort.",
