   "start_page": 2,
   "summary": "This enclosure consists of an explanatory introduction and a ten-page directory of 169 public, academic, and industrial libraries across the United States and Canada holding material on Japan. Authored by R. L. Tuthill, the explanatory preface outlines the criteria used to select economic, military, and scientific publications, the adoption of Hepburn romanization (romaji) and English translations for Japanese titles, the card cataloguing system, and the exclusion of U.S. Government Printing Office materials. The accompanying 'Numerical List of Libraries' serves as the master key linking the index numbers assigned to each bibliographic card to the specific repository where the item is held.",
   "title": "Enclosure: Explanation and Numerical List of Libraries for the Bibliography of Japonica",
